  <data key="d8">CREB2; activating transcription factor 4</data>
</node>
<node id="ATG16L1_COMPLEX">
  <data key="d1">ATG16L1_COMPLEX</data>
  <data key="d2">ATG12–ATG5–ATG16L1 complex</data>
  <data key="d3">complex</data>
  <data key="d4">mtorc1_output_autophagy_metabolism_feedback</data>
  <data key="d5">6</data>
  <data key="d6">E3-like conjugation machinery recruited to PI3P-positive phagophores by WIPI2; lipidates LC3/GABARAP proteins onto the expanding autophagosomal membrane.</data>
  <data key="d7"></data>
  <data key="d8">ATG16L1 conjugation complex</data>
</node>
<node id="ATG9A">
  <data key="d1">ATG9A</data>
  <data key="d2">ATG9A</data>
  <data key="d3">protein</data>
  <data key="d4">mtorc1_output_autophagy_metabolism_feedback</data>
  <data key="d5">6</data>
  <data key="d6">The only transmembrane core autophagy protein; a lipid scramblase delivered in vesicles that seed the phagophore, trafficked under ULK1 control.</data>
  <data key="d7">ATG9A</data>
  <data key="d8">mATG9</data>
</node>
<node id="BECN1">
  <data key="d1">BECN1</data>
  <data key="d2">Beclin-1</data>
  <data key="d3">protein</data>
  <data key="d4">mtorc1_output_autophagy_metabolism_feedback</data>
  <data key="d5">6</data>
  <data key="d6">Core subunit of class III PI3K complexes; ULK1 phosphorylation at Ser14 activates VPS34 lipid-kinase output for phagophore nucleation.</data>
  <data key="d7">BECN1</data>
  <data key="d8">ATG6</data>
</node>
<node id="CAD">
  <data key="d1">CAD</data>
  <data key="d2">CAD</data>
  <data key="d3">protein</data>
  <data key="d4">mtorc1_output_autophagy_metabolism_feedback</data>
  <data key="d5">6</data>
  <data key="d6">Trifunctional pyrimidine-synthesis enzyme; included here as an S6K1 substrate (Ser1859) to complete the S6K1 substrate set. Cross-reference to the metabolism module.</data>
  <data key="d7">CAD</data>
  <data key="d8">CAD enzyme</data>
</node>
<node id="CEBPB">
  <data key="d1">CEBPB</data>
  <data key="d2">C/EBPβ (CEBPB)</data>
  <data key="d3">protein</data>
  <data key="d4">mtorc1_output_autophagy_metabolism_feedback</data>
  <data key="d5">6</data>
  <data key="d6">Rhythmically expressed transcription factor that times the autophagy gene programme in liver; provides a mechanistic basis for rhythmic autophagic flux.</data>
  <data key="d7">CEBPB</data>
  <data key="d8">C/EBP beta</data>
</node>
<node id="FASN">
  <data key="d1">FASN</data>
  <data key="d2">Fatty acid synthase</data>
  <data key="d3">protein</data>
  <data key="d4">mtorc1_output_autophagy_metabolism_feedback</data>
  <data key="d5">6</data>
  <data key="d6">one of the lipogenic genes induced downstream of mTORC1–SREBP1.</data>
  <data key="d7">FASN</data>
  <data key="d8">FAS</data>
</node>
<node id="G6PD">
  <data key="d1">G6PD</data>
  <data key="d2">G6PD</data>
  <data key="d3">protein</data>
  <data key="d4">mtorc1_output_autophagy_metabolism_feedback</data>
  <data key="d5">6</data>
  <data key="d6">Rate-limiting enzyme of the oxidative pentose phosphate pathway, induced through SREBP downstream of mTORC1; supplies NADPH and ribose-5-phosphate.</data>
  <data key="d7">G6PD</data>
  <data key="d8">glucose-6-phosphate dehydrogenase</data>
</node>
<node id="GLUD1">
  <data key="d1">GLUD1</data>
  <data key="d2">glutamate dehydrogenase</data>
  <data key="d3">protein</data>
  <data key="d4">mtorc1_output_autophagy_metabolism_feedback</data>
  <data key="d5">6</data>
  <data key="d6">Mitochondrial enzyme converting glutamate to alpha-ketoglutarate for TCA anaplerosis; activated downstream of mTORC1-S6K1 through repression of SIRT4.</data>
  <data key="d7">GLUD1</data>
  <data key="d8">GDH</data>
</node>
<node id="HK2">
  <data key="d1">HK2</data>
  <data key="d2">hexokinase 2</data>
  <data key="d3">protein</data>
  <data key="d4">mtorc1_output_autophagy_metabolism_feedback</data>
  <data key="d5">6</data>
  <data key="d6">Mitochondria-associated hexokinase; an mTORC1/HIF-1 transcriptional output that, when free of glucose-6-phosphate during glucose deprivation, binds Raptor via a TOS-like motif and inhibits mTORC1 to promote autophagy.</data>
