  <data key="d13">Luminal amino acids act through the v-ATPase, in a manner requiring its ATP hydrolysis, to weaken its interaction with Ragulator at the V1 sector without changing lysosomal pH; this conformational relay is the first step of inside-out signalling to the Rag GTPases.</data>
  <data key="d14">established</data>
  <data key="d15"></data>
  <data key="d16">708</data>
