<edge source="CHOLESTEROL" target="SLC38A9" id="lipid_binding:8a49feffbc986c6e">
  <data key="d9">CHOLESTEROL</data>
  <data key="d10">SLC38A9</data>
  <data key="d11">lipid_binding</data>
  <data key="d12">activates</data>
  <data key="d13">SLC38A9 senses lysosomal cholesterol through conserved cholesterol-responsive motifs in its transmembrane region; this sterol input, separable from arginine sensing, drives Rag-dependent recruitment and activation of mTORC1.</data>
  <data key="d14">emerging</data>
  <data key="d15"></data>
  <data key="d16">92</data>
  <data key="d17"></data>
  <data key="d18">upstream_of_mTORC1</data>
  <data key="d19">The arginine-sensing and transport roles of SLC38A9 are well established, whereas the cholesterol arm is still emerging.</data>
  <data key="d20">lysosomal_nutrient_sensing</data>
  <data key="d21">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="GDP" target="RRAGC" id="binding:f1ab77b0d4b7e160">
  <data key="d9">GDP</data>
  <data key="d10">RRAGC</data>
  <data key="d11">binding</data>
  <data key="d12">activates</data>
  <data key="d13">RagC/D must be GDP-loaded for the asymmetric, mTORC1-competent configuration; RagC.GTP yields the inactive heterodimer</data>
