  <data key="d13">NPRL2 loss of function causes familial focal epilepsy of the GATOR1 spectrum through unopposed RagA/B-GTP loading and mTORC1 hyperactivity, with a focal cortical malformation in a minority of patients. In a small open-label series of NPRL2- and NPRL3-related epilepsy, add-on everolimus reduced seizures in all four patients treated, two of whom became seizure-free, although stomatitis led one patient to stop treatment.</data>
