  <data key="d12">activates</data>
  <data key="d13">Mechanical stretch and eccentric contraction were reported to raise phosphatidic acid in skeletal muscle through phospholipase D, independently of ERK and PI3K; later work from the same laboratory found that phospholipase D activity does not rise with loading and that the mechanically induced phosphatidic acid depends on diacylglycerol kinase zeta.</data>
