  <data key="d10">EVEROLIMUS</data>
  <data key="d11">other</data>
  <data key="d12">modulates</data>
  <data key="d13">Genotype within the GATOR1 complex appears to influence everolimus response in the familial focal epilepsies: in an open-label series, patients with DEPDC5 loss-of-function variants showed substantial seizure reduction, a patient with a DEPDC5 missense variant responded less, and the single NPRL3 patient worsened, whereas a later series in NPRL2- and NPRL3-related epilepsy reported seizure reduction in all four treated patients. The evidence is open-label and very small, and a controlled trial is required before this becomes practice.</data>
  <data key="d14">emerging</data>
