<edge source="VAR_NPRL3_LOF" target="DISEASE_GATOR1_EPILEPSY" id="genetic_loss_of_function:6e44db045cac88a3">
  <data key="d9">VAR_NPRL3_LOF</data>
  <data key="d10">DISEASE_GATOR1_EPILEPSY</data>
  <data key="d11">genetic_loss_of_function</data>
  <data key="d12">activates</data>
  <data key="d13">NPRL3 loss of function causes familial focal epilepsy of the GATOR1 spectrum through unopposed RagA/B-GTP loading and mTORC1 hyperactivity in the cortical lesion. Responses to add-on everolimus have differed between series: the single NPRL3 patient in the first case series worsened, whereas all four patients in a later NPRL2- and NPRL3-related series improved, two of them becoming seizure-free.</data>
  <data key="d14">established</data>
  <data key="d15"></data>
  <data key="d16">22; 84; 417; 494</data>
  <data key="d17">germline heterozygous</data>
  <data key="d18">pathophysiological</data>
  <data key="d19">The small open-label series do not establish NPRL3 genotype as a predictor of everolimus failure, and a controlled trial is required before mTOR inhibition becomes standard practice.</data>
  <data key="d20">lysosomal_nutrient_sensing</data>
  <data key="d21">1</data>
</edge>
