<edge source="VAR_STK11_LOF" target="MTORC1" id="other:6df23304c94db020">
  <data key="d9">VAR_STK11_LOF</data>
  <data key="d10">MTORC1</data>
  <data key="d11">other</data>
  <data key="d12">activates</data>
  <data key="d13">Loss-of-function STK11/LKB1 lesions abolish energy-stress-induced Thr172 phosphorylation of AMPK, removing both the TSC2-GAP and the Raptor Ser792 brakes, so mTORC1 is no longer restrained when ATP falls; Ca2+-driven Thr172 phosphorylation by CaMKK2 is retained, and growth-factor and amino-acid control of mTORC1 persists.</data>
  <data key="d14">established</data>
  <data key="d15"></data>
  <data key="d16">138; 375; 546; 624</data>
  <data key="d17">STK11-mutant tumours; Peutz-Jeghers syndrome</data>
  <data key="d18">pathophysiological</data>
  <data key="d19">A single-arm trial of everolimus in advanced solid tumours selected for TSC1, TSC2, NF1, NF2 or STK11 mutations showed no meaningful single-agent activity, so such a lesion marks an enriched population rather than demonstrated dependence on the kinase.</data>
  <data key="d20">energy_stress_input</data>
  <data key="d21">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="VAR_STK11_LOF" target="STK11" id="genetic_loss_of_function:b392b85a20e79a96">
