  <data key="d12">inhibits</data>
  <data key="d13">Class I PI3K inhibition lowers PIP3 and therefore both AKT recruitment and mSin1-dependent mTORC2 activation. In a randomised comparison with everolimus in renal cell carcinoma, apitolisib produced shorter progression-free survival and markedly more high-grade hyperglycaemia and rash, illustrating the toxicity ceiling that limited dual PI3K-mTOR inhibitors developed to pre-empt feedback reactivation.</data>
