  <data key="d11">physiological_output</data>
  <data key="d12">activates</data>
  <data key="d13">Calcineurin inhibitors block calcineurin-NFAT signalling in the pancreatic beta cell, reducing insulin secretion and beta-cell mass and producing new-onset diabetes after transplantation, with tacrolimus carrying the higher risk of the two agents. This mechanism is distinct from the direct beta-cell toxicity and mTORC2-dependent peripheral insulin resistance associated with sirolimus.</data>
  <data key="d14">established</data>
