  <data key="d13">Everolimus lowers mTORC1-dependent phosphorylation of 4E-BP1 and so favours sequestration of eIF4E, but suppression is site-selective: Ser65 and Thr70, which require prior priming and sustained mTORC1 activity, are suppressed, whereas the priming sites Thr37 and Thr46 remain largely phosphorylated. Cap-dependent translation of messages with structured 5' untranslated regions is therefore only partly inhibited.</data>
