  <data key="d10">PHENO_CNS_DRUG_EXPOSURE</data>
  <data key="d11">physiological_output</data>
  <data key="d12">activates</data>
  <data key="d13">RapaLink-1 crosses the blood-brain barrier and accumulates in intracranial tumour tissue to a degree the first- and second-generation agents do not, which is the basis of its preclinical activity in glioblastoma models.</data>
  <data key="d14">emerging</data>
  <data key="d15"></data>
