</edge>
<edge source="RAPAMYCIN" target="DISEASE_CANCER" id="drug_inhibition:565da1689b69b360">
  <data key="d9">RAPAMYCIN</data>
  <data key="d10">DISEASE_CANCER</data>
  <data key="d11">drug_inhibition</data>
  <data key="d12">inhibits</data>
  <data key="d13">Sirolimus-class agents have real but largely cytostatic antitumour activity: albumin-bound sirolimus is approved for advanced malignant perivascular epithelioid cell tumour, with response enriched in TSC2-mutant tumours, while no randomised trial of a rapalog in a solid tumour has shown a significant overall survival benefit. Separately, deferral of lethal neoplasia may account for part of the lifespan extension rapamycin produces in mice.</data>
  <data key="d14">established</data>
  <data key="d15"></data>
  <data key="d16">432; 633</data>
  <data key="d17">advanced solid tumours; mouse lifespan studies</data>
  <data key="d18">pathophysiological</data>
  <data key="d19">What is disputed is the mechanism of murine lifespan extension, not the existence of antitumour activity.</data>
  <data key="d20">tissue_physiology_disease</data>
  <data key="d21">-1</data>
</edge>
