  <data key="d13">Rapamycin protects dopaminergic neurons in cellular and rodent models of Parkinson disease; in those models protection tracked with blocked production of the stress protein RTP801/REDD1 and preserved AKT phosphorylation, whereas the catalytic inhibitor Torin1 was not protective. Enhanced autophagic clearance of alpha-synuclein is a separate route shown in other model systems.</data>
