  <data key="d13">Non-infectious pneumonitis occurs in roughly 5-15% of oncology patients treated with rapalogs and is the most serious and least well understood toxicity of the class. It is probably immune-mediated rather than a direct consequence of mTORC1 blockade in lung epithelium, and management rests on vigilance, dose interruption and discontinuation.</data>
