<edge source="RMC5552" target="EIF4EBP1" id="drug_inhibition:bc9f744aa0a490c8">
  <data key="d9">RMC5552</data>
  <data key="d10">EIF4EBP1</data>
  <data key="d11">drug_inhibition</data>
  <data key="d12">activates</data>
  <data key="d13">RMC-5552 tethers an FKBP12-rapamycin moiety to an ATP-site moiety; FKBP12-mediated avidity confers mTORC1 selectivity while the ATP-site moiety blocks catalysis. Phosphorylation of 4E-BP1 at all four sites, including the rapamycin-resistant priming sites Thr37 and Thr46, is therefore suppressed, and hypophosphorylated 4E-BP1 binds eIF4E. The activation of the repressor is indirect, through inhibition of mTORC1 kinase activity.</data>
  <data key="d14">established</data>
  <data key="d15">Ser65; Thr37; Thr46; Thr70</data>
  <data key="d16">69; 339</data>
  <data key="d17"></data>
  <data key="d18">pharmacological</data>
  <data key="d19">Whether complete suppression of 4E-BP1 phosphorylation translates into genotype-dependent clinical benefit is not yet established.</data>
  <data key="d20">mtorc1_output_translation_ribosome</data>
  <data key="d21">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="RMC5552" target="RPS6KB1" id="drug_inhibition:8fd68922cd8eaabc">
