  <data key="d10">RPS6KB1</data>
  <data key="d11">drug_inhibition</data>
  <data key="d12">inhibits</data>
  <data key="d13">The bi-steric design tethers an FKBP12-rapamycin moiety to an ATP-site moiety; FKBP12-mediated avidity confers mTORC1 selectivity while the ATP-site moiety delivers complete catalytic inhibition, so both S6K1 Thr389 and 4E-BP1 are fully suppressed while mTORC2 is relatively spared.</data>
  <data key="d14">established</data>
  <data key="d15">Thr389</data>
  <data key="d16">69; 339</data>
  <data key="d17"></data>
  <data key="d18">pharmacological</data>
  <data key="d19">RMC-5552 suppresses both S6K1 and 4E-BP1 phosphorylation fully while relatively sparing mTORC2. The effect on S6K1 is indirect, through inhibition of mTORC1 kinase activity.</data>
  <data key="d20">mtorc1_output_translation_ribosome</data>
  <data key="d21">-1</data>
</edge>
