  <data key="d12">modulates</data>
  <data key="d13">ATP-competitive mTOR inhibition regulates AKT biphasically. Catalytic blockade of mTORC2 abolishes Ser473 phosphorylation and suppresses AKT activity acutely; relief of S6K1-IRS-1 and Grb10 feedback then drives receptor tyrosine kinase-dependent PI3K signalling, so Thr308 phosphorylation and AKT activity rebound while Ser473 phosphorylation remains suppressed.</data>
  <data key="d14">established</data>
  <data key="d15">Ser473; Thr308</data>
  <data key="d16">500</data>
  <data key="d17">class effect of ATP-competitive mTOR inhibitors</data>
  <data key="d18">feedback</data>
  <data key="d19">The rebound is a principal reason why superior pathway suppression did not translate into clinical efficacy for this class.</data>
  <data key="d20">pharmacology</data>
  <data key="d21">0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="SAPANISERTIB" target="EIF4EBP1" id="drug_inhibition:ea63df52f7e34445">
