  <data key="d11">drug_inhibition</data>
  <data key="d12">activates</data>
  <data key="d13">ATP-competitive occupancy of the mTOR kinase cleft suppresses phosphorylation of all four principal 4E-BP1 sites, including Thr37 and Thr46, which allosteric rapalogs leave largely intact. Hypophosphorylated 4E-BP1 is the active form, so eIF4E is sequestered and cap-dependent translation of mRNAs with structured 5' untranslated regions is blocked.</data>
  <data key="d14">established</data>
  <data key="d15">Ser65; Thr37; Thr46; Thr70</data>
  <data key="d16">166; 246; 603</data>
  <data key="d17"></data>
  <data key="d18">downstream_of_mTORC1</data>
  <data key="d19">Indirect activation of the translational repressor through reduced mTORC1-dependent phosphorylation; the drug does not directly activate 4E-BP1.</data>
  <data key="d20">pharmacology</data>
  <data key="d21">1</data>
</edge>
