<edge source="TORIN1" target="CAP_DEPENDENT_TRANSLATION" id="drug_inhibition:7ef509b96a5a4eb5">
  <data key="d9">TORIN1</data>
  <data key="d10">CAP_DEPENDENT_TRANSLATION</data>
  <data key="d11">drug_inhibition</data>
  <data key="d12">inhibits</data>
  <data key="d13">ATP-competitive occupancy of the mTOR kinase cleft suppresses the rapamycin-resistant 4E-BP1 Thr37/Thr46 sites, so 4E-BP1 remains eIF4E-bound, eIF4F does not assemble, and cap-dependent initiation is blocked far more completely than with rapamycin.</data>
  <data key="d14">established</data>
  <data key="d15"></data>
  <data key="d16">166; 603; 604</data>
  <data key="d17"></data>
  <data key="d18">pharmacological</data>
  <data key="d19"></data>
  <data key="d20">mtorc1_output_translation_ribosome</data>
  <data key="d21">-1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="TORIN1" target="EIF4EBP1" id="drug_inhibition:bc3539a69fb8934d">
  <data key="d9">TORIN1</data>
  <data key="d10">EIF4EBP1</data>
  <data key="d11">drug_inhibition</data>
  <data key="d12">activates</data>
  <data key="d13">By occupying the ATP site of mTOR, Torin1 blocks phosphorylation of 4E-BP1 at all four sites, including the priming sites Thr37 and Thr46 that resist rapamycin, and cellular phosphatases then remove the existing phosphates. Hypophosphorylated 4E-BP1 sequesters eIF4E, so the activation of the repressor is indirect, through inhibition of the mTOR kinase.</data>
  <data key="d14">established</data>
  <data key="d15">Ser65; Thr37; Thr46; Thr70</data>
  <data key="d16">166; 603</data>
  <data key="d17"></data>
  <data key="d18">pharmacological</data>
  <data key="d19">Complete suppression of 4E-BP1 phosphorylation requires catalytic-site rather than allosteric inhibition. Other ATP-competitive mTOR inhibitors act the same way, among them PP242, KU-0063794 and AZD8055; sapanisertib and vistusertib belong to the same class.</data>
  <data key="d20">mtorc1_output_translation_ribosome</data>
  <data key="d21">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="TORIN1" target="RPS6KB1" id="drug_inhibition:bad1a50a06da50f7">
  <data key="d9">TORIN1</data>
  <data key="d10">RPS6KB1</data>
  <data key="d11">drug_inhibition</data>
  <data key="d12">inhibits</data>
  <data key="d13">ATP-competitive mTOR inhibition abolishes S6K1 Thr389 phosphorylation together with the rapamycin-resistant outputs of mTORC1, so mTORC1 signalling is suppressed completely rather than partially. The effect on S6K1 is indirect, through inhibition of the mTOR kinase.</data>
  <data key="d14">established</data>
  <data key="d15">Thr389</data>
  <data key="d16">166; 603</data>
  <data key="d17"></data>
  <data key="d18">pharmacological</data>
  <data key="d19"></data>
  <data key="d20">mtorc1_output_translation_ribosome</data>
  <data key="d21">-1</data>
</edge>
