  <data key="d10">PHENO_HYPERGLYCAEMIA</data>
  <data key="d11">physiological_output</data>
  <data key="d12">activates</data>
  <data key="d13">Complete inhibition of mTORC2 by ATP-competitive agents produces hyperglycaemia through combined beta-cell dysfunction and peripheral insulin resistance, with mTORC2 contributing more than mTORC1; this metabolic ceiling limited clinical development of the class.</data>
  <data key="d14">emerging</data>
  <data key="d15"></data>
  <data key="d16">325; 568</data>
  <data key="d17">class-level attribution; vistusertib-specific incidence not reported</data>
  <data key="d18">pathophysiological</data>
  <data key="d19">Hyperglycaemia is reported across ATP-competitive mTOR inhibitors; no incidence specific to vistusertib is available.</data>
  <data key="d20">pharmacology</data>
  <data key="d21">1</data>
</edge>
