<edge source="SESN2" target="AMPK" id="other:9671563fb5a9e207">
  <data key="d9">SESN2</data>
  <data key="d10">AMPK</data>
  <data key="d11">other</data>
  <data key="d12">activates</data>
  <data key="d13">Sestrins have been reported to activate AMPK and so to inhibit mTORC1 through TSC2, a route independent of GATOR2 sequestration; the molecular basis is undefined and Sestrin2 still suppresses mTORC1 in AMPK-null cells.</data>
  <data key="d14">emerging</data>
  <data key="d15"></data>
  <data key="d16">65; 337</data>
  <data key="d17"></data>
  <data key="d18">upstream_of_mTORC1</data>
  <data key="d19">The AMPK arm is reported rather than reproduced; the best-supported route from Sestrin2 to mTORC1 is sequestration of GATOR2.</data>
  <data key="d20">lysosomal_nutrient_sensing</data>
  <data key="d21">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="SESN2" target="AMPK" id="binding:835685a5266d7a21">
  <data key="d9">SESN2</data>
  <data key="d10">AMPK</data>
  <data key="d11">binding</data>
  <data key="d12">activates</data>
  <data key="d13">Sestrin1/2 were reported to bind AMPK (and TSC2) and promote AMPK-mediated TSC2 phosphorylation, mediating p53-dependent mTORC1 inhibition after genotoxic stress.</data>
  <data key="d14">contested</data>
  <data key="d15"></data>
  <data key="d16">65</data>
  <data key="d17">DNA damage; genotoxic stress</data>
  <data key="d18">upstream_of_mTORC1</data>
  <data key="d19">Later work (Chantranupong 2014, Peng 2014 Cell) shows sestrins inhibit mTORC1 primarily through GATOR2 and the Rag GTPases, independently of AMPK; the physiological contribution of the AMPK route is disputed.</data>
  <data key="d20">energy_stress_input</data>
  <data key="d21">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="SESN2" target="GATOR2" id="sequestration:8e5ea12c95e6f2b6">
  <data key="d9">SESN2</data>
  <data key="d10">GATOR2</data>
  <data key="d11">sequestration</data>
  <data key="d12">inhibits</data>
  <data key="d13">Apo-Sestrin2 binds GATOR2 across the WDR24 and SEH1L beta-propellers, with auxiliary contacts to MIOS, preventing GATOR2 from inhibiting GATOR1 so RagA/B remain GDP-bound and mTORC1 leaves the lysosome; leucine binding (Kd approximately 20 microM) releases GATOR2.</data>
  <data key="d14">established</data>
  <data key="d15"></data>
  <data key="d16">94; 530; 581; 655</data>
  <data key="d17">leucine deprivation</data>
  <data key="d18">upstream_of_mTORC1</data>
  <data key="d19">Established in vitro and structurally, while the physiological primacy of Sestrin2 as a leucine sensor is contested. Sestrin2 is itself induced by p53 and ATF4, so stress input converges on this step.</data>
  <data key="d20">lysosomal_nutrient_sensing</data>
  <data key="d21">-1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="SESN2" target="RRAGA" id="other:4b5390c1b33a4eb8">
  <data key="d9">SESN2</data>
  <data key="d10">RRAGA</data>
  <data key="d11">other</data>
  <data key="d12">inhibits</data>
  <data key="d13">Alternative model in which Sestrin2 acts as a guanine-nucleotide dissociation inhibitor for RagA/B, locking them in the GDP state, rather than acting only by sequestering GATOR2. Published results conflict with the GATOR2-sequestration-only model.</data>
  <data key="d14">contested</data>
  <data key="d15"></data>
  <data key="d16">337; 460</data>
  <data key="d17"></data>
  <data key="d18">upstream_of_mTORC1</data>
  <data key="d19">Contested: the guanine-nucleotide dissociation inhibitor model and the GATOR2-sequestration model of Sestrin action are in direct conflict and have not been reconciled.</data>
  <data key="d20">lysosomal_nutrient_sensing</data>
  <data key="d21">-1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="SESN2" target="WDR24" id="binding:e3ab2a3ce2797937">
  <data key="d9">SESN2</data>
  <data key="d10">WDR24</data>
  <data key="d11">binding</data>
  <data key="d12">inhibits</data>
  <data key="d13">Sestrin2 binds the WDR24-SEH1L region of GATOR2; MIOS is the principal CASTOR1-binding subunit.</data>
  <data key="d14">emerging</data>
  <data key="d15"></data>
  <data key="d16">581; 618</data>
  <data key="d17"></data>
  <data key="d18">upstream_of_mTORC1</data>
  <data key="d19"></data>
  <data key="d20">lysosomal_nutrient_sensing</data>
  <data key="d21">-1</data>
</edge>
