  <data key="d12">modulates</data>
  <data key="d13">GTP-bound H-Ras and K-Ras (predominantly KRAS4A) bind the atypical Ras-binding domain of mSin1. Oncogenic Ras was reported to promote mTORC2 activity at the plasma membrane, but a Sin1 mutant unable to bind Ras supports normal mTORC2 assembly and activity in cells and mice, and Sin1 overexpression was reported to suppress Ras signalling.</data>
  <data key="d14">contested</data>
  <data key="d15"></data>
  <data key="d16">91; 318; 537</data>
  <data key="d17">shown chiefly with oncogenic KRAS/HRAS in cultured cells</data>
  <data key="d18">upstream_of_mTORC2</data>
  <data key="d19">The consequence of Ras binding for mTORC2 activity is disputed between laboratories. The Ras-binding domain is one of the defined mSin1 regions, but no function has been firmly assigned to it.</data>
  <data key="d20">growth_factor_input</data>
  <data key="d21">0</data>
</edge>
