  <data key="d16">187; 216; 226</data>
  <data key="d17"></data>
  <data key="d18">upstream_of_mTORC1</data>
  <data key="d19">The LKB1-STRADalpha-MO25 heterotrimer is the physiological AMPK kinase; STRADalpha and MO25 are required for LKB1 catalytic competence and cytoplasmic localisation.</data>
  <data key="d20">energy_stress_input</data>
  <data key="d21">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="MITOCHONDRIAL_COMPLEX_I" target="ATP" id="other:eef0880935854231">
  <data key="d9">MITOCHONDRIAL_COMPLEX_I</data>
  <data key="d10">ATP</data>
  <data key="d11">other</data>
  <data key="d12">required_for</data>
  <data key="d13">Complex I oxidises NADH and pumps protons, sustaining the proton-motive force that ATP synthase uses, so complex I activity is required for maximal oxidative ATP production rather than converting a substrate into ATP. Biguanide inhibition of complex I therefore lowers ATP and raises AMP and ADP, the classical high-dose route to AMPK activation.</data>
  <data key="d14">established</data>
  <data key="d15"></data>
  <data key="d16">235; 442</data>
  <data key="d17">biguanide exposure</data>
  <data key="d18">upstream_of_mTORC1</data>
  <data key="d19"></data>
  <data key="d20">energy_stress_input</data>
  <data key="d21">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="PEN2" target="ATP6AP1" id="binding:2b48ed0e89f9345e">
  <data key="d9">PEN2</data>
  <data key="d10">ATP6AP1</data>
  <data key="d11">binding</data>
  <data key="d12">inhibits</data>
  <data key="d13">Metformin-bound PEN2 binds the v-ATPase accessory subunit ATP6AP1 and inhibits the lysosomal v-ATPase, triggering AXIN–LKB1-dependent activation of lysosomal AMPK at clinically relevant metformin concentrations and without a fall in cellular ATP.</data>
  <data key="d14">emerging</data>
  <data key="d15"></data>
  <data key="d16">372</data>
  <data key="d17">low-dose metformin</data>
  <data key="d18">pharmacological</data>
  <data key="d19">Completes the low-dose metformin route from PEN2 through v-ATPase inhibition to lysosomal AMPK activation; reported by a single laboratory (Ma T et al., Nature 2022;603:159-165).</data>
  <data key="d20">energy_stress_input</data>
  <data key="d21">-1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="PEX5" target="TSC2" id="recruitment:952e252484b6eb1d">
  <data key="d9">PEX5</data>
  <data key="d10">TSC2</data>
