<edge source="FLCN_FNIP" target="TFEB" id="other:13133b88789ccf01">
  <data key="d9">FLCN_FNIP</data>
  <data key="d10">TFEB</data>
  <data key="d11">other</data>
  <data key="d12">inhibits</data>
  <data key="d13">FLCN-FNIP loads RagC/D with GDP, which is specifically required for mTORC1 to phosphorylate TFEB at Ser211 and keep it cytoplasmic; FLCN loss therefore leaves TFEB nuclear while S6K1 and 4E-BP1 phosphorylation are preserved.</data>
  <data key="d14">established</data>
  <data key="d15"></data>
  <data key="d16">429; 610</data>
  <data key="d17">Birt-Hogg-Dube kidney</data>
  <data key="d18">downstream_of_mTORC1</data>
  <data key="d19">The effect on TFEB is indirect, exerted through the Rag heterodimer, and explains the tissue-dependent rather than uniform mTORC1 phenotype of FLCN loss.</data>
  <data key="d20">lysosomal_nutrient_sensing</data>
  <data key="d21">-1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="FNIP1" target="AMPK" id="binding:f128047bcb1c4a1b">
