  <data key="d10">RRAGA</data>
  <data key="d11">gef_activity</data>
  <data key="d12">activates</data>
  <data key="d13">Ragulator was reported to act as a guanine nucleotide exchange factor for RagA/B (Bar-Peled 2012), but later reconstitution found that it chiefly triggers GTP release from RagC, with SLC38A9 acting as the GEF for RagA.</data>
  <data key="d14">contested</data>
  <data key="d15"></data>
  <data key="d16">27; 556</data>
  <data key="d17"></data>
  <data key="d18">upstream_of_mTORC1</data>
  <data key="d19">Shen and Sabatini (2018) attribute the original RagA/B result to assay limitations, including possibly copurifying SLC38A9, while noting that Ragulator still alters the GTP affinity of RagA.</data>
  <data key="d20">lysosomal_nutrient_sensing</data>
  <data key="d21">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="RAGULATOR" target="AXIN1" id="recruitment:4f442e5f0ac7e7c6">
