</edge>
<edge source="RNF152" target="RHEB" id="ubiquitination:3281827163423206">
  <data key="d9">RNF152</data>
  <data key="d10">RHEB</data>
  <data key="d11">ubiquitination</data>
  <data key="d12">inhibits</data>
  <data key="d13">The lysosomal E3 ligase RNF152 mono-ubiquitinates Rheb at Lys8, increasing its affinity for the TSC complex and suppressing mTORC1; EGF stimulation acts through AKT-phosphorylated USP4, which deubiquitinates Rheb and releases it from the complex.</data>
  <data key="d14">emerging</data>
  <data key="d15">Lys8</data>
  <data key="d16">136</data>
  <data key="d17">growth-factor withdrawal</data>
  <data key="d18">upstream_of_mTORC1</data>
  <data key="d19">Reported by a single laboratory and not independently replicated in vivo; the same group identified RNF152 as the E3 ligase for RagA.</data>
  <data key="d20">growth_factor_input</data>
  <data key="d21">-1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="RUVBL1" target="TTT_COMPLEX" id="binding:dab4af04a734c231">
  <data key="d9">RUVBL1</data>
  <data key="d10">TTT_COMPLEX</data>
  <data key="d11">binding</data>
  <data key="d12">required_for</data>
  <data key="d13">RUVBL1 (Pontin) binds the Tel2-Tti1-Tti2 module as part of the R2TP co-chaperone, whose PIH1D1 subunit recognises CK2-phosphorylated Tel2. The ATP-dependent TTT-RUVBL1/2 assembly is needed for mTOR stability, mTORC1 dimerisation and mTORC1 binding to the Rag GTPases.</data>
  <data key="d14">established</data>
  <data key="d15"></data>
  <data key="d16">239; 311</data>
  <data key="d17"></data>
  <data key="d18">upstream_of_mTORC1</data>
  <data key="d19">RUVBL1 is not a subunit of TTT itself, which comprises Tel2, Tti1 and Tti2; energy depletion disassembles the TTT-RUVBL1/2 complex.</data>
  <data key="d20">lysosomal_nutrient_sensing</data>
  <data key="d21">1</data>
</edge>
