  <data key="d13">RUVBL2 (Reptin) binds the Tel2-Tti1-Tti2 module together with RUVBL1 as part of the R2TP co-chaperone, whose PIH1D1 subunit recognises CK2-phosphorylated Tel2. The ATP-dependent TTT-RUVBL1/2 assembly is needed for mTOR stability, mTORC1 dimerisation and mTORC1 binding to the Rag GTPases.</data>
