<edge source="VAR_FLCN_LOF" target="TFEB" id="other:c864e4faf4c161d8">
  <data key="d9">VAR_FLCN_LOF</data>
  <data key="d10">TFEB</data>
  <data key="d11">other</data>
  <data key="d12">activates</data>
  <data key="d13">Without FLCN GAP activity RagC/D remains GTP-bound, so mTORC1 cannot phosphorylate TFEB at Ser211 even though it phosphorylates S6K1 and 4E-BP1 normally, and TFEB accumulates constitutively in the nucleus; removing TFEB rescues the renal phenotype of kidney-specific Flcn-knockout mice, indicating that this substrate-selective lesion rather than global mTORC1 hyperactivity drives it.</data>
  <data key="d14">established</data>
  <data key="d15">Ser211</data>
  <data key="d16">429; 534; 610</data>
  <data key="d17">FLCN-null renal epithelium</data>
  <data key="d18">pathophysiological</data>
  <data key="d19">Consistent with the tissue-dependent rather than uniformly increased mTORC1 signalling seen in Birt-Hogg-Dube syndrome.</data>
  <data key="d20">lysosomal_nutrient_sensing</data>
  <data key="d21">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="VAR_FLCN_LOF" target="FLCN_FNIP" id="genetic_loss_of_function:91d1fa2e1abe1f18">
