  <data key="d12">activates</data>
  <data key="d13">TCTP was proposed as a Rheb guanine-nucleotide exchange factor in Drosophila; subsequent biochemical studies found no GEF activity.</data>
  <data key="d14">contested</data>
  <data key="d15"></data>
  <data key="d16">247; 491; 639</data>
  <data key="d17"></data>
  <data key="d18">upstream_of_mTORC1</data>
  <data key="d19">Rheb's high intrinsic GTP loading makes a guanine-nucleotide exchange factor dispensable, and TSC2 GAP activity is treated as the sole regulator of its nucleotide state. Graded contested because the original Drosophila report is directly contradicted by later biochemistry.</data>
  <data key="d20">growth_factor_input</data>
  <data key="d21">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="TSC1" target="TSC2" id="stabilisation:93e89a95bdb339d7">
