<edge source="TSC_COMPLEX" target="RHEB" id="gap_activity:3b00efdaa774e4d6">
  <data key="d9">TSC_COMPLEX</data>
  <data key="d10">RHEB</data>
  <data key="d11">gap_activity</data>
  <data key="d12">inhibits</data>
  <data key="d13">The TSC1–TSC2–TBC1D7 complex (2:2:1) presents the TSC2 GAP domain at its apex to lysosomal Rheb and accelerates GTP hydrolysis ~100-fold; in the absence of insulin the complex is held on the lysosome through Rheb and is released when AKT phosphorylates TSC2.</data>
  <data key="d14">established</data>
  <data key="d15"></data>
  <data key="d16">143; 261; 407; 600; 673</data>
  <data key="d17">lysosomal surface</data>
  <data key="d18">upstream_of_mTORC1</data>
  <data key="d19">The complex is the GAP and inactivates Rheb; loss of TSC1 or TSC2 leaves Rheb GTP-loaded and mTORC1 constitutively active. Lysosomal retention of the complex and its insulin-dependent release were shown by Menon and colleagues.</data>
  <data key="d20">growth_factor_input</data>
  <data key="d21">-1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="TSC_COMPLEX" target="MTORC2" id="binding:57848355f3937bec">
  <data key="d9">TSC_COMPLEX</data>
  <data key="d10">MTORC2</data>
  <data key="d11">binding</data>
  <data key="d12">activates</data>
  <data key="d13">The TSC1–TSC2 complex physically associates with mTORC2 and promotes its activity toward AKT, independently of its Rheb GAP function.</data>
  <data key="d14">emerging</data>
  <data key="d15"></data>
  <data key="d16">249</data>
  <data key="d17"></data>
  <data key="d18">upstream_of_mTORC2</data>
  <data key="d19">Polarity is opposite to the TSC-mTORC1 relationship.</data>
  <data key="d20">mtorc2_regulation_and_outputs</data>
  <data key="d21">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="AMPK" target="MTORC1" id="other:19780ba05a14a845">
  <data key="d9">AMPK</data>
  <data key="d10">MTORC1</data>
  <data key="d11">other</data>
  <data key="d12">inhibits</data>
  <data key="d13">Activated AMPK inhibits mTORC1 by two routes: phosphorylation of TSC2, which enhances its GAP activity toward Rheb, and direct phosphorylation of Raptor at Ser722 and Ser792, which creates 14-3-3 binding sites and imposes a metabolic checkpoint.</data>
  <data key="d14">established</data>
  <data key="d15"></data>
  <data key="d16">187; 207; 216; 226; 262</data>
  <data key="d17">energy stress</data>
  <data key="d18">upstream_of_mTORC1</data>
  <data key="d19">Net effect of the TSC2 and Raptor phosphorylation routes rather than a separate molecular event.</data>
  <data key="d20">energy_stress_input</data>
  <data key="d21">-1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="AMPK" target="MTORC2" id="phosphorylation:3b0f0a72203f7d79">
  <data key="d9">AMPK</data>
  <data key="d10">MTORC2</data>
  <data key="d11">phosphorylation</data>
  <data key="d12">activates</data>
  <data key="d13">During acute energetic stress AMPK phosphorylates mTOR and Rictor within mTORC2, increasing mTORC2 activity toward AKT Ser473 and promoting cell survival, independently of its inhibition of mTORC1.</data>
  <data key="d14">emerging</data>
  <data key="d15"></data>
  <data key="d16">300</data>
  <data key="d17">acute energetic stress (glucose deprivation, AICAR)</data>
  <data key="d18">upstream_of_mTORC2</data>
  <data key="d19">Single-laboratory study. In vitro, AMPK phosphorylated mTOR at Ser1261 and Rictor at unmapped sites, but Ser1261 was not required for AMPK-induced mTORC2 signalling, so the functionally relevant sites are unknown.</data>
  <data key="d20">energy_stress_input</data>
  <data key="d21">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="AMPK" target="RPTOR" id="phosphorylation:028c01ca53886639">
  <data key="d9">AMPK</data>
  <data key="d10">RPTOR</data>
  <data key="d11">phosphorylation</data>
  <data key="d12">inhibits</data>
  <data key="d13">AMPK directly phosphorylates Raptor at two conserved serines, creating 14-3-3 binding sites that reduce mTORC1 kinase activity; imposes a metabolic checkpoint (G2/M arrest) independent of TSC2.</data>
  <data key="d14">established</data>
  <data key="d15">Ser722; Ser792</data>
  <data key="d16">187; 207; 216; 226; 262</data>
  <data key="d17">energy stress</data>
  <data key="d18">upstream_of_mTORC1</data>
  <data key="d19">Both Raptor sites, including Ser792, are needed for the full checkpoint.</data>
  <data key="d20">energy_stress_input</data>
  <data key="d21">-1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="AMPK" target="RPTOR" id="phosphorylation:7ed08e694fcfc5d1">
  <data key="d9">AMPK</data>
  <data key="d10">RPTOR</data>
