  <data key="d12">inhibits</data>
  <data key="d13">During amino-acid starvation Rag-Ragulator traps FLCN-FNIP2 in the inactive lysosomal folliculin complex (LFC), holding FLCN's catalytic arginine finger away from the RagC nucleotide pocket; amino-acid refeeding releases the complex and licenses RagC/D GTP hydrolysis. This checkpoint explains why FLCN GAP activity is nutrient-gated.</data>
  <data key="d14">established</data>
  <data key="d15"></data>
  <data key="d16">331; 468; 557</data>
  <data key="d17">amino-acid starvation</data>
  <data key="d18">upstream_of_mTORC1</data>
  <data key="d19">Two independent cryo-EM structures (Lawrence 2019; Shen 2019) show FLCN-FNIP2 bound to RagA-GDP with the FLCN catalytic arginine away from the RagC nucleotide; Shen 2019 interprets this state as an on-pathway intermediate rather than an inhibitory trap.</data>
  <data key="d20">lysosomal_nutrient_sensing</data>
  <data key="d21">-1</data>
</edge>
