  <data key="d10">MTOR</data>
  <data key="d11">binding</data>
  <data key="d12">component_of</data>
  <data key="d13">The N-terminal HEAT repeats, arranged as N-HEAT (horn) and M-HEAT (bridge) segments, fold into an elongated alpha-solenoid. The solenoid contributes to the dimer interface and provides the docking surface for Raptor in mTORC1 and Rictor in mTORC2.</data>
  <data key="d14">established</data>
  <data key="d15"></data>
  <data key="d16">14; 588; 670</data>
  <data key="d17"></data>
  <data key="d18">core</data>
  <data key="d19">Domain-level decomposition of mTOR</data>
  <data key="d20">core_complexes</data>
  <data key="d21">0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="KINASE_DOMAIN" target="MTOR" id="binding:717076bca7f5292f">
  <data key="d9">KINASE_DOMAIN</data>
  <data key="d10">MTOR</data>
  <data key="d11">binding</data>
  <data key="d12">component_of</data>
  <data key="d13">PI3K-like catalytic domain carrying the ATP site in a deeply recessed cleft; it is the catalytic unit shared by mTORC1, mTORC2 and the putative mTORC3.</data>
  <data key="d14">established</data>
  <data key="d15"></data>
  <data key="d16">315; 588; 670</data>
  <data key="d17"></data>
  <data key="d18">core</data>
