<edge source="MAPKAP1" target="AKT" id="scaffolding:ec425e8ee1ba35bc">
  <data key="d9">MAPKAP1</data>
  <data key="d10">AKT</data>
  <data key="d11">scaffolding</data>
  <data key="d12">required_for</data>
  <data key="d13">mTORC2 selects AKT by distal docking: the basic surface of the AKT kinase N-lobe engages an acidic loop of the mSin1 CRIM domain and the C-lobe a Rictor–mSin1 mooring ~75 Å from the active site; residues flanking Ser473 are dispensable, and prior engagement of pThr450 by the same N-lobe residues builds in a proofreading step.</data>
  <data key="d14">emerging</data>
  <data key="d15"></data>
  <data key="d16">74; 483; 597</data>
  <data key="d17"></data>
  <data key="d18">core</data>
  <data key="d19">The primary support is the 2025 enzyme-substrate structure [597]; the 'conserved tri-arginine cluster' formulation is inaccurate and should be avoided. The claim rests on this single structural study, with [74,483] as supporting cellular observations.</data>
  <data key="d20">growth_factor_input</data>
  <data key="d21">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="MAPKAP1" target="AKT" id="binding:46cce357dfc70865">
  <data key="d9">MAPKAP1</data>
  <data key="d10">AKT</data>
  <data key="d11">binding</data>
  <data key="d12">required_for</data>
  <data key="d13">The basic surface of the Akt kinase N-lobe engages an acidic loop of the mSin1 CRIM domain ~75 A from the catalytic site; specificity is structural, not local sequence around Ser473.</data>
  <data key="d14">emerging</data>
  <data key="d15"></data>
  <data key="d16">597</data>
  <data key="d17"></data>
  <data key="d18">core</data>
  <data key="d19">Primary support is a single 2025 structural study; the widely repeated 'tri-arginine cluster' formulation should be treated with caution.</data>
  <data key="d20">core_complexes</data>
  <data key="d21">1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="MAPKAP1" target="AKT" id="scaffolding:1473922a369acb07">
  <data key="d9">MAPKAP1</data>
  <data key="d10">AKT</data>
  <data key="d11">scaffolding</data>
  <data key="d12">required_for</data>
  <data key="d13">An acidic loop of the mSin1 CRIM domain engages the basic AKT N-lobe surface ~75 Å from the catalytic site, encoding substrate choice by distal docking rather than local sequence.</data>
  <data key="d14">emerging</data>
  <data key="d15">mSin1 CRIM domain acidic loop</data>
  <data key="d16">74; 597</data>
  <data key="d17"></data>
  <data key="d18">core</data>
  <data key="d19">Residues flanking Ser473 are unimportant for phosphorylation. The same N-lobe residues engage phospho-Thr450, so AKT must change conformation first, which builds a proofreading step into substrate selection. The distal-docking geometry rests on a single structural study.</data>
  <data key="d20">mtorc2_regulation_and_outputs</data>
  <data key="d21">1</data>
</edge>
