  <data key="d12">inhibits</data>
  <data key="d13">mTORC1 phosphorylates 4E-BP2 at Thr37, Thr46, Ser65 and Thr70, the residues equivalent to the 4E-BP1 sites, in a rapamycin-sensitive manner that releases eIF4E. Loss of both 4E-BP1 and 4E-BP2 makes TOP and TOP-like mRNA translation resistant to mTOR inhibition.</data>
