  <data key="d12">inhibits</data>
  <data key="d13">In proliferating cells with high mTORC1 activity, ATF4 (CREB2) protein has been reported to undergo proteasome-dependent degradation, lowering SIRT4 transcription and thereby relieving SIRT4-mediated inhibition of glutamate dehydrogenase.</data>
  <data key="d14">contested</data>
