</edge>
<edge source="MTORC2" target="TIAM1" id="physiological_output:d3e17d0744041cd7">
  <data key="d9">MTORC2</data>
  <data key="d10">TIAM1</data>
  <data key="d11">physiological_output</data>
  <data key="d12">activates</data>
  <data key="d13">Forebrain mTORC2 promotes Rac1 activation through Tiam1 and the resulting actin polymerisation in dendritic spines, rather than acting through translational control; conditional Rictor deletion in postnatal forebrain selectively impairs late-phase LTP and long-term memory while sparing early-phase LTP and short-term memory.</data>
  <data key="d14">established</data>
  <data key="d15"></data>
  <data key="d16">250</data>
  <data key="d17">postnatal murine forebrain</data>
  <data key="d18">downstream_of_mTORC2</data>
  <data key="d19">The structural, actin-dependent arm of this division of labour has been demonstrated chiefly by one laboratory, in mice and flies.</data>
  <data key="d20">tissue_physiology_disease</data>
  <data key="d21">1</data>
</edge>
