  <data key="d11">physiological_output</data>
  <data key="d12">modulates</data>
  <data key="d13">Muscle-specific Rictor deletion is close to phenotypically silent, in contrast to Raptor deletion, which causes dystrophy; the residual mTORC2 contribution is limited to loss of AKT Ser473 phosphorylation and a modest fall in insulin-stimulated glucose uptake.</data>
