  <data key="d11">physiological_output</data>
  <data key="d12">modulates</data>
  <data key="d13">Loss of both mTOR complexes in CD4 T cells favours Foxp3+ regulatory T cell differentiation; an independent contribution of mTORC2 to this restraint, acting through AKT, is supported but less consistently than the mTORC1 arm.</data>
  <data key="d14">emerging</data>
