  <data key="d9">PRR5L</data>
  <data key="d10">RICTOR</data>
  <data key="d11">binding</data>
  <data key="d12">modulates</data>
  <data key="d13">Protor-2 (PRR5L), the paralogue of Protor-1, binds Rictor and thereby associates with mTORC2 without being required for complex integrity or kinase activity; a binding site shared with Protor-1 and strictly exclusive binding of the two paralogues have not been mapped.</data>
