</edge>
<edge source="BTRC" target="DEPTOR" id="ubiquitination:04841a685ee61501">
  <data key="d9">BTRC</data>
  <data key="d10">DEPTOR</data>
  <data key="d11">ubiquitination</data>
  <data key="d12">inhibits</data>
  <data key="d13">SCF-betaTrCP binds the phosphorylated DEPTOR degron and polyubiquitinates it, committing the inhibitory subunit to proteasomal degradation.</data>
  <data key="d14">established</data>
  <data key="d15"></data>
  <data key="d16">150; 186; 701</data>
  <data key="d17"></data>
  <data key="d18">feedback</data>
  <data key="d19"></data>
  <data key="d20">core_complexes</data>
  <data key="d21">-1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="BTRC" target="DEPTOR" id="degradation:6e1414cfcc3bd24f">
  <data key="d9">BTRC</data>
  <data key="d10">DEPTOR</data>
  <data key="d11">degradation</data>
  <data key="d12">inhibits</data>
  <data key="d13">Growth-factor-induced phosphorylation of the DEPTOR degron, primed by mTOR (or by S6K1 and RSK1) and completed by casein kinase 1 alpha, creates a betaTrCP binding site; SCF-betaTrCP then ubiquitinates DEPTOR and targets it for proteasomal degradation, so active mTOR removes its own inhibitor.</data>
  <data key="d14">established</data>
  <data key="d15"></data>
  <data key="d16">150; 186; 701</data>
  <data key="d17"></data>
  <data key="d18">core</data>
  <data key="d19"></data>
  <data key="d20">mtorc1_output_autophagy_metabolism_feedback</data>
  <data key="d21">-1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="BTRC" target="SCF_BTRC" id="complex_formation:5b760f411bed13dc">
  <data key="d9">BTRC</data>
  <data key="d10">SCF_BTRC</data>
  <data key="d11">complex_formation</data>
  <data key="d12">component_of</data>
  <data key="d13">beta-TrCP1 is the F-box substrate-receptor subunit of the SCF ligase that destroys DEPTOR.</data>
  <data key="d14">established</data>
  <data key="d15"></data>
  <data key="d16">150; 186; 701</data>
  <data key="d17"></data>
  <data key="d18">core</data>
  <data key="d19"></data>
  <data key="d20">core_complexes</data>
  <data key="d21">0</data>
</edge>
